# AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/generators/gen_solar_sites.py - do not edit manually.
### Solar System Colonization's per-world and per-slot rows, from
### gen_solar_sites.SITES (slices 2-3 design §§ 3, 8, 10). The row types are in
### space_race_widget.gui: te_sr_site_row (Solar System, every world under its
### location, in panel_order(), filtered by default), te_sr_colony_row
### (Colonies, every world, shown while ours; audit SPC-5), te_sr_cf_slot_row
### (Colony Fleets, one per fleet slot), te_sr_mq_row (the Modules view's queue,
### one per place), te_sr_free_row (the Autonomy view's Free Colonies, every
### world, shown while free; slice 5 design § 9) and te_sr_window_row (Mission
### Control's Next Windows, one per destination, sr_launch_window_widgets.gui;
### colony management design § 6). Each value is a display value
### of sr_sites_display_generated.txt (the Defenses view's, of
### sr_fleets_display_generated.txt), the scripted GUIs are in sr_colony_sguis.txt.
### te_sr_cede_site_list_war and _treaty are Cede Colony's picker, the worlds the
### ceding country holds by location; its tile, te_sr_cede_site_tile, is in
### right_click_menu.gui. te_sr_target_picker_rows is the colony target popup's
### list (UI pass design § 5): every world by location, with its launch window,
### Target button and people room, filtered to the worlds we can target by default.
### te_sr_colony_brief_rows is another country's Colonies (National Info):
### every world, shown while the shown Country holds it, read on Country,
### with nothing to press (te_sr_colony_brief_row). The Colonies window
### (te_sr_colony_popup; the owner, 2026-11-23) takes te_sr_colony_switch_rows,
### its list of our colonies, and te_sr_colony_pages, a page a world
### (te_sr_colony_page) filled from its row's blocks. te_sr_map_locations is the
### system map's nine columns (te_sr_map_location), each with its sites'
### markers (te_sr_map_pip); a location picked there (sr_ss_loc) lists that
### location alone in te_sr_solar_system_rows.

types sr_sites_generated_rows_types
{
